WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.140
Not everything you see in movies is real,
but it’s hard to fake chemistry… or is

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.929
it? These co-stars prove that you don’t
have to actually like someone to convince

00:00:08.929 --> 00:00:13.200
the world you’re BFFs. What’s a little
leg licking between friends? You’ll have

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.849
to watch to the end to find out.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:20.250
During the filming of "The Fate of the Furious"
there was an alleged beef between two of the

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.870
film's biggest stars: Vin Diesel and Dwayne
"The Rock" Johnson.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:28.230
"Just like in life you have different philosophies
and people have different philosophies - different

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:32.210
fundamental philosophies on how you do things
- and again, the most important thing is just

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.270
the movies."

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:37.960
After the production, Johnson took to social
media to praise only some of his co-stars,

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:39.570
writing in a since deleted post -

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:44.811
"My female co stars are always amazing, and
I love 'em. My male co stars, however, are

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:49.010
a different story. Some conduct themselves
as stand-up men and true professionals, while

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.350
others don't."

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:54.510
Although it was unclear exactly who The Rock
was referring to, the aim of that jab most

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.989
likely included Diesel.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:58.899
Diesel addressed it to clear the air, telling
USA Today -

00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:03.570
"I don't think the world really realizes how
close we are, in a weird way. I think some

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.569
things may be blown out of proportion. [...] In
my house, he's Uncle Dwayne."

00:01:08.569 --> 00:01:12.649
Allegedly, Ryan Reynolds had trouble with
Wesley Snipes during the filming of 2004's

00:01:12.649 --> 00:01:17.350
"Blade: Trinity." But then again, apparently
so did the entire cast and crew.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:21.069
Journalist Chris Parry, who at the time was
working on an article about the production

00:01:21.069 --> 00:01:26.060
of the film, spent some time on the set and
spoke to crew members anonymously. One source

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.600
talked about Snipes and Reynolds' relationship,
saying -

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:34.450
"He refers to Ryan Reynolds as 'that c------'
or 'tell that c------ to get out of my eyeline,'

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.600
and 'tell that c------ to get his lines right.'"

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:41.029
Snipes reportedly was difficult with everyone
on set, and there have been rumors that he

00:01:41.029 --> 00:01:46.289
even at one point strangled the film's director,
David Goyer. According to The Hollywood Reporter,

00:01:46.289 --> 00:01:49.060
Goyer never confirmed the incident but he
did say -

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:54.090
"I have tremendous respect for Wesley as an
actor. He used to be a friend. We're not friends

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:57.859
anymore. I don't think anyone involved in
that film had a good experience; certainly,

00:01:57.859 --> 00:01:58.859
I didn't."

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.429
2000's "Charlie's Angels" was a box office
hit, bolstered by a star-studded cast that

00:02:04.429 --> 00:02:08.869
included Cameron Diaz, Drew Barrymore, and
Lucy Liu as the Angels, and Bill Murray as

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:13.260
the pseudo-manager, Bosley. However, in reality
the team didn't seem as connected as they

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:14.590
did in the movie.

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:19.150
The story goes that there was a rewrite of
one scene, and Murray wasn't happy with it.

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:23.000
For some reason, he took his frustration out
on Liu — despite her claiming not to have

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.040
anything to do with the changes. She addressed
the incident during an interview on the Los

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.269
Angeles Times podcast "Asian Enough." According
to Liu, Murray began insulting her, and she

00:02:32.269 --> 00:02:33.540
didn't back down. She said -

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:37.950
"I stood up for myself, and I don't regret
it. Because no matter how low on the totem

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:42.519
pole you may be or wherever you came from,
there's no need to condescend or to put other

00:02:42.519 --> 00:02:43.519
people down."

00:02:43.519 --> 00:02:48.010
The two have seemingly rekindled their professional
relationship, but Liu still thinks she did

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:49.829
the right thing in standing up to Murray.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:54.849
It's hard to pinpoint the exact reason for
the longstanding feud between "Sex and the

00:02:54.849 --> 00:02:59.000
City" co-stars Sarah Jessica Parker and Kim
Cattrall, but it's clear that the two weren't

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.269
the best of friends on set. In an interview
with Piers Morgan, Cattrall explained why

00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:09.329
she didn't want to return for the reboot series,
saying she had been portrayed as "demanding

00:03:09.329 --> 00:03:12.739
or a diva" in the press. She also singled
out Parker's behavior.

00:03:12.739 --> 00:03:19.360
"I think she could have been nicer. I really
think she could have been nicer. I don't know

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.270
what her issue is."

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:25.709
Tensions escalated later when, after a death
in the family, Cattrall posted a message to

00:03:25.709 --> 00:03:28.590
her Instagram directed at Parker; it read:

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:33.030
"Your continuous reaching out is a painful
reminder of how cruel you really were then

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:38.110
and now. Let me make this VERY clear. (If
I haven't already.) You are not my family.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:43.189
You are not my friend. So I'm writing to tell
you one last time to stop exploiting our tragedy

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:46.049
in order to restore your 'nice girl' persona."

00:03:46.049 --> 00:03:49.910
At the same time, Parker has maintained that
she never had it out for Cattrall, saying

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:50.910
to Elle -

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:55.230
"I don't think anybody wants to believe that
I love Kim. I adore her. I wouldn't have done

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.230
the movie without her."

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:01.519
One of Meryl Streep's first starring roles
was alongside another current veteran, Dustin

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:06.549
Hoffman, in 1979's "Kramer vs. Kramer." And
Streep claimed to the New York Times that

00:04:06.549 --> 00:04:08.269
Hoffman went too far while filming.

00:04:08.269 --> 00:04:12.490
The incident happened during a scene in which
Hoffman's character slapped Streep's, and

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:16.609
apparently the slap was a little too real.
Referring to the scene, Streep said -

00:04:16.609 --> 00:04:21.740
"This is tricky because when you're an actor,
you're in a scene, you have to feel free.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:25.510
I'm sure that I have inadvertently hurt people
in physical scenes. [...] But this was my

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:30.551
first movie, and it was my first take in my
first movie, and he just slapped me. And you

00:04:30.551 --> 00:04:31.980
see it in the movie."

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.170
For Hoffman's part, he did admit that he was
difficult to work with during the production,

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.370
and that his problems in his personal life
affected his coworkers on set.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:44.430
Although they teamed up onscreen, Jim Carrey
and Tommy Lee Jones weren't quite partners

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:49.950
in crime on the set of 1995's "Batman Forever,"
and much of that animosity came from Jones.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:54.001
According to Carrey, there was one incident
that spoke to Jones' feelings about him. During

00:04:54.001 --> 00:04:57.530
an appearance on the late Norm MacDonald's
talkshow, Carrey explained that during a day

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:01.461
off while filming the movie, the two happened
to be sitting in the same restaurant. Carrey

00:05:01.461 --> 00:05:05.470
decided to go over and say hello, which apparently
wasn't something Jones wanted.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:14.520
"And he went to hug me and said, 'I hate you.
I really don't like you.'"

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.430
Carrey then asked what the problem was, and
said -

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:21.633
"I pulled up a chair, which probably wasn't
smart, and he said, 'I cannot sanction your buffoonery.'"

00:05:21.633 --> 00:05:26.220
Of course, as The Riddler, Carrey's character
came with a certain amount of 'buffoonery.'

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:30.770
But apparently the man behind the green, question-marked
jumpsuit had a little too much silliness on-set

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:31.770
for Jones' liking.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:38.140
Marlon Brando and Sophia Loren starred alongside
each other in the 1967 Charlie Chaplin-directed

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:43.540
comedy "A Countess from Hong Kong." According
to Loren, Brando got a bit too touchy-feely,

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:46.410
and she responded by letting him know that
was not okay.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:50.380
She explained in her autobiography, "Yesterday,
Today, Tomorrow: My Life," writing -

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:54.650
"All of a sudden, he put his hands on me.
I turned in all tranquility and blew in his

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:59.710
face, like a cat stroked the wrong way and
said, 'Don't you ever dare to do that again.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:00.710
Never again!'"

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.990
Although Brando didn't do anything like that
again while filming the movie, it made the

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:08.250
rest of the production uncomfortable for Loren.
She admitted that it was difficult to work

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.250
with him afterwards.

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:13.750
Gene Kelly's "Singin' In The Rain" co-star
Debbie Reynolds revealed that the twosome's

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:17.760
working relationship was much more fraught
than their onscreen rapport. She wrote in

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:18.760
her memoir -

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:23.910
"He came to rehearsals and criticized everything
I did and never gave me a word of encouragement,"

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:27.270
Reynolds continued that, when it was time
to shoot the kissing scenes with Kelly, things

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.190
got even more uncomfortable, writing -

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:33.761
"Gene took me tightly in his arms [...] and
shoved his tongue down my throat. 'Eeew! What

00:06:33.761 --> 00:06:37.490
was that?' I screeched, breaking free of his
grasp and spitting."

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:42.870
And to make matters a bit more awkward, Reynolds
was just 19 at the time, while Kelly was 37.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:43.870
Reynolds went on to write -

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:48.120
"I was an innocent kid who had never been
French-kissed. It felt like an assault."

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:54.270
Behind the scenes of 1983's "Terms of Endearment,"
there were rumors about how tension between

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:59.540
Shirley MacLaine and Debra Winger manifested
on set in some very strange ways. During an

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:04.190
appearance on "Watch What Happens Live," Winger
was asked about rumors that she tried to pass

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:08.450
gas towards MacLaine or that she licked her
leg while the latter was trying to film a

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:09.860
love scene with Jack Nicholson.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:13.430
"Was any of that true?"
"You mean you wanna just go in there and say

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.950
is there something true in there?"
"Yeah."

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.870
"There's something true in there."

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:21.960
Despite the fighting, the duo of acting greats
still hold each other in high regard — at

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.830
least professionally, with Winger telling
The New York Times -

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:28.720
"I can't deny that we fought. [...] But I
think there was always a respect between the

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:29.720
two of us."

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:34.820
The grudge match between Hollywood icons Bette
Davis and Joan Crawford is so legendary that

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:39.560
it was turned into a TV show in 2017, aptly
titled "Feud: Bette and Joan."

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:45.490
So, what was the issue? Well, a lot of things.
The two reportedly fought over nearly everything,

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:50.000
including lovers, movie roles, fame, and parenting
— all before ever working together. It all

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:54.720
came to a head when the duo starred alongside
each other in 1962's "What Ever Happened to

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:58.050
Baby Jane?" Entertainment Weekly writes that
Davis once said -

00:07:58.050 --> 00:08:03.070
"The best time I ever had with Joan Crawford
was when I pushed her down the stairs."

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:06.980
In a scene, in which Davis was supposed to
fake kick Crawford in the head, she actually

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:10.310
did make contact, and it resulted in three
stitches.

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:13.870
But Crawford got her revenge during a scene
where Davis had to pull her out of bed. Crawford

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:17.780
secretly wore a heavy weightlifter's belt
underneath her costume, knowing that Davis

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:19.590
had a bad back.

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:24.560
Even when Crawford died in 1977 of a heart
attack, the fight lived on. Upon hearing of

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.870
her rival's passing, Davis allegedly said
-

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:32.400
"You should never say bad things about the
dead, only good. Joan Crawford is dead. Good."

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:37.820
Kenny Baker and Anthony Daniels, better known
as their iconic characters R2-D2 and C-3PO

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:43.800
respectively, weren't as close as their iconic
onscreen bond made it seem. Baker has publicly

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:47.890
said that Daniels disrespected him on-set
by calling him insulting names.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:52.990
Daniels responded to the claims, telling his
side of the story in 2019 to the Daily Express,

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:53.990
saying -

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:58.400
"Kenny decided that he wanted to say unkind,
unpleasant, rude, hurtful things. It got worse

00:08:58.400 --> 00:08:59.400
and worse."

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:04.020
When the suits came on, however, it was all
business and easy to put aside their differences.

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:05.020
Daniels explained -

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:10.340
"The fact is we didn't really appear or interact
together. He was in a box he couldn't do anything

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:13.490
with. He couldn't hear me. He never made a
sound."

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:17.430
Check out one of our newest videos right here!
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:21.120
on screen partners are coming soon. Subscribe
to our YouTube channel and hit the bell so

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:21.800
you don't miss a single one.

